  "mechanism": "Red diagonal point pairs have length4, blue side point pairs have length sqrt(8). The specific predicted error is mixing the two point-pair roles and demanding that all emphasized pair lengths be equal for a square, falsely concluding no square (A). The real square requires equality only of its four boundary sides; its diagonals are correctly longer by sqrt(2).",
